@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: draft
+entities: [Comment, CommentReport]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/CommentController.ts
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/CommentResource.ts
+  - app/Policies/CommentPolicy.ts
+  - db/schema.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-code/fable-5-1", at: 2026-09-29T15:09:14.742Z }
+---
+
+# Hide comments reported by three users
+
+## Context
+
+Readers can comment on posts, and nobody moderates on call. Product will
+not ship comments that one bad actor can fill with spam, so the community
+has to be able to clear a comment away on its own, and one person alone
+must not be able to.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Any signed-in user can report a comment. `comment_reports` holds one row
+  per report, and the pair (`comment_id`, `user_id`) is unique, so
+  reporting again changes nothing and the row count is the number of
+  different reporters.
+- A comment with `REPORTS_TO_HIDE` (3) or more reports is left out of the
+  post page for every viewer, its author and the post's author included.
+  `Comment.visibleOn()` is the one place that decides this.
+- Hidden is derived from the report rows on every read. Nothing on
+  `comments` stores it, so a report written or removed by review tooling
+  takes effect without a second write.
+- A hidden comment stays in `comments` for review. Deleting is separate
+  and physical: the comment's author or the post's author removes the row
+  and its reports, and deleting a post removes its comments with it.
+- `Comment.purge()` deletes reports and comments itself. The foreign keys
+  also declare `ON DELETE CASCADE`, but SQLite enforces foreign keys only
+  on a connection that turned them on, which the app does not do.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Three accounts acting together can hide any comment, and nothing in the
+  app brings it back: there is no review screen yet, so un-hiding means
+  deleting rows from `comment_reports` by hand.
+- The post page runs one grouped count over the reports of the post's
+  comments on each view. A post with a very large number of comments will
+  want pagination before it wants a stored flag.
+- Reporting answers 204 whether the report is new or a repeat, so the
+  page cannot tell a user they had already reported a comment.
